data/cache/
# utdata/ and data/blog/ are ignored by default, so analysis runs and figure uploads never show up as untracked files.
# The files that ARE tracked under them were added on purpose with `git add -f` (git keeps tracking a file once it is
# added, whatever .gitignore says) and belong to the published record:
#   utdata/  the scripts, inputs and results behind published or drafted articles and the model checks:
#            Edda (+ Edda/kallor), Malt, blindtest, blogg (+ blogg/build, blogg/forslag), forslag, huggspar, kallor,
#            landning, lda_kategorier, luckartikel, material, mi, modellartikel, ordpar, ristare (+ ristare/ut),
#            runlm_forfining (+ runlm_forfining/tm19), skane, sparlasare, sprakprov, stilgrupp_ai
#   data/blog/figures/  two article figures that article scripts and saved article versions in utdata/blogg refer to
# A new file there that should be kept is added with `git add -f <path>`; list tracked ones with `git ls-files utdata`.
utdata/
/.next/
data/raa/
data/ortnamn/
data/dk/fortidsminder.csv
data/blog/
data/github/

# The public website's trial build (scripts: see .github/workflows/site.yml)
.site-build/
examples/*/ut/

# Earlier versions of the articles, written before every save and deletion (api/routers/blog.py)
data/backup/
# Local copies kept before a model generation replaced a data file (e.g. data/runlm_calibration.json.fore-tm19-2026-10-20);
# the record of each generation is in utdata/runlm_forfining. Add one with `git add -f` if it should be kept.
data/*.fore-*

# Playwright (web/e2e)
web/test-results/
web/playwright-report/
